   "top": {
    "Each stone represents the time of the construction of the section where the people of Yeongdong-gun in Chungcheong-do were in charge of the construction. ": 1,
    "Explanation: The section of the city wall at which the repair work was commenced by the military government of Hongsan, Chungcheong-do Province, in 1422 (4th year of King Sejong&apos;s reign) ": 1,
    "Location: outside the wall - near the Dongdaemun Seonggwak Park (site of Dongdaemun Church) ": 1,
    "Explanation: The area in which the 13th construction work commenced at the time of Seoul City Wall construction in 1396 (5th year of King Taejo&apos;s reign). Sueum means &quot;&quot;to receive&quot;&quot; and &quot;&quot;to finish things swiftly (with one breath). ": 1,
    "Explanation: A section containig 600 units of 崑字 (gonja) of Cheonjamun Okchulgongang, the 47th out of the 97 sections from the peak of Bugaksan Baegakmaru that were built during the construction of Seoul City Wall in 1396 (5th year of King Taejo&apos;s reign). ": 1,
    "Explanation: In Oct. 1804 (4th year of King Sunjo&apos;s reign), Paejang Oh Jae-min, Gamgwan Yi Dong-han and Pyeonsu Yong Seong-hwi were involved in the repair work. ": 1
